   "source": [
    "### Description for each column"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b038a430-b11a-481f-ade6-c9a1059a4259",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. kepid: A unique identifier for each exoplanet in the dataset.\n",
    "2. kepoi_name: The name assigned to the Kepler Object of Interest (KOI), representing a potential exoplanet.\n",
    "3. koi_disposition: The status of the exoplanet (0 for confirmed, 1 for candidate, 2 for rejected).\n",
    "4. koi_score: A score between 0 and 1 indicating the confidence level that the object is a true exoplanet.\n",
    "5. koi_period: The orbital period of the exoplanet in days.\n",
    "6. koi_prad: The radius of the exoplanet in Earth radii.\n",
    "7. koi_teq: The equilibrium temperature of the exoplanet in Kelvin.\n",
    "8. koi_insol: The amount of stellar flux received by the exoplanet, measured in Earth insolation units.\n",
    "9. koi_steff: The effective temperature of the host star in Kelvin.\n",
    "10. koi_srad: The radius of the host star in solar radii.\n",
    "11. koi_slogg: The surface gravity of the host star in logarithmic units.\n",
    "12. koi_kepmag: The apparent magnitude of the host star in the Kepler band, indicating its brightness."
   ]
  },
